// Title: Write Protect For Storage Disabled
// Sigma ID: 75f7a0e2-7154-4c4d-9eae-5cdb4e0a5c13
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sreeman
// Date: 2021-06-11 | Modified: 2024-01-18
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects applications trying to modify the registry in order to disable any write-protect
//   property for storage devices. This could be a precursor to a ransomware attack and has been an
//   observed technique used by cypherpunk group.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.manageengine.com/products/desktop-central/os-imaging-deployment/media-is-write-protected.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_write_protect_for_storage_disabled.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Write Protection" and ProcessCommandLine contains "0" and ProcessCommandLine contains "storage"
